<description>&lt;p&gt;Islamist militants abducted 14 Islamic school students in Niger State while bandits demanded over ₦100 million ransom for them, and gunmen killed four civilians and wounded five in a north-central market. Russian electronic-warfare vehicles were observed operating in Mali, indicating foreign military involvement, and Benin President Wadagni reshuffled military leadership after a failed coup. Human Rights Watch reported that Islamist armed groups in Burkina Faso are targeting civilians, and the conflict caused 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirAFBVV95cUxPOUhjT1BycHBYSDdnWkhWSXk5NngwbWJWYThyUmpaVF9PZXdXSDk1c1RfZm0tNGNrQVNHeGNJZ19nekhscEQ3RC0tSFFqRWJnOTM0QlFza09NaE5tT0ItUHlRSnpIaFVtTFAtcFV3Yk9sekp2Z1M2LVRzRUxEYncyLWxVT2RNRGozeVdPcXMwNlNVQjItVzVxODFoUDNwTVFmazVDWndjLXR1Wjlw?oc=5&quot;&gt;FIJ NG&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxNOE00YXBGVGdGS21mSTUtWGlscVRJQ251NFdHN3JEOGI0TGE3b1ppOFV2RmRZRXBHZ0tZa3NzR1NaR1hpcDJGaTRURHhhdVRzNVgyajRhUjF6T3dTcDFOWFI3ME1oQjZyYzBhcWJhakpZLTg0X29sYi1VS3VBNkNReUNyNEFxVS1sNTRvdHRUNlhzNnFYTDVqSnc3N1pZX2dqd2NEbEpadnlZUl9WdXU3bQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Straits Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxQbmF6QmQtUUVja3l4U1daUVRyV2hUd2NqZjRXdHFYTDdmN2V6WjE4SktPQmMyQkh4RTdEbW1xSVlGVnVPM3hUOVBSdm45R2hwbVpUNTdOTzhVcE1HaWpaQ1lKZks2Wk44OVBFV3Z4LXhHcmZaZk1ZSl9nWEdqSlR4bWR0QXg5emJJSHRnRmNEQ1BUQW5PZ1pJTUp0ck5hblJWVGxOXzNGTmtQZVR2Q18zaFo2Zmxhdw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Premium Times Nigeria&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Vanguard News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiwFBVV95cUxQa1R4Y1Vka2dzbFhsYWNCRGszaE15c1MwWHk1MU5LUDBsZUhpSTBXbEFtZmxSUk5WMS1Ga0todFVMcUlOSDNHblNVWEhKdVYtaFNUN0V1